{
  "articles": [
    {
      "id": "sj-01-forms",
      "title": "Step 1: The subjunctive: regular forms",
      "fr": "le subjonctif présent : les formes",
      "level": "B1",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "subjunctive",
        "subjonctif",
        "que je",
        "forms",
        "ils parlent"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "subjonctif-basics"
      ],
      "tense": "subjonctif-present",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "The subjunctive (*subjonctif*) is a verb form used after certain expressions, almost always after **que**: *Il faut que tu viennes.* To form it, take the **ils** form of the present, drop **-ent**, and add *-e, -es, -e, -ions, -iez, -ent*."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "ils (present)",
                "stem",
                "subjunctive"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "ils parlent",
                  "parl-",
                  "que je parle"
                ],
                [
                  "ils finissent",
                  "finiss-",
                  "que je finisse"
                ],
                [
                  "ils attendent",
                  "attend-",
                  "que j'attende"
                ],
                [
                  "ils partent",
                  "part-",
                  "que je parte"
                ],
                [
                  "ils écrivent",
                  "écriv-",
                  "que j'écrive"
                ],
                [
                  "ils disent",
                  "dis-",
                  "que je dise"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Take ils, drop -ent",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "verb": "finir",
              "tense": "subjonctif-present"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "For *-er* verbs *je, tu, il, ils* look like the present: *que je parle*. You see the difference with *-ir* and *-re* verbs: *que je finisse, que je parte*."
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "form",
                "verb": "attendre",
                "tense": "subjonctif-present",
                "person": 0
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Nous and vous: like the imparfait",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Nous* and *vous* take the stem of *nous* in the present, so they look like the imparfait: *que nous parlions, que vous finissiez*. Verbs with two stems show it clearly: *que je prenne / que nous prenions, que je vienne / que nous venions, que je boive / que nous buvions*."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "verb": "prendre",
              "tense": "subjonctif-present"
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "form",
                "verb": "prendre",
                "tense": "subjonctif-present",
                "person": 3
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Il faut que je parte.",
                  "en": "I have to leave."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Je veux que tu finisses ton assiette.",
                  "en": "I want you to finish your plate."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il faut que vous écriviez la lettre.",
                  "en": "You have to write the letter."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Le prof veut que nous lisions ce livre.",
                  "en": "The teacher wants us to read this book."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
