    {
      "id": "sj-02-irregular",
      "title": "Step 2: Irregular subjunctives",
      "fr": "le subjonctif irrégulier",
      "level": "B1",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "subjunctive",
        "irregular",
        "sois",
        "aie",
        "aille",
        "fasse",
        "puisse",
        "sache",
        "veuille"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "subjonctif-basics"
      ],
      "tense": "subjonctif-present",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Seven common verbs are irregular. Learn them as a group: **être, avoir, aller, faire, pouvoir, savoir, vouloir**. Two impersonal ones are also useful: *qu'il faille* (falloir), *qu'il pleuve* (pleuvoir)."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "verb",
                "que je",
                "que nous"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "être",
                  "sois",
                  "soyons"
                ],
                [
                  "avoir",
                  "aie",
                  "ayons"
                ],
                [
                  "aller",
                  "aille",
                  "allions"
                ],
                [
                  "faire",
                  "fasse",
                  "fassions"
                ],
                [
                  "pouvoir",
                  "puisse",
                  "puissions"
                ],
                [
                  "savoir",
                  "sache",
                  "sachions"
                ],
                [
                  "vouloir",
                  "veuille",
                  "voulions"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Être and avoir",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "verb": "être",
              "tense": "subjonctif-present"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "verb": "avoir",
              "tense": "subjonctif-present"
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "cloze",
                "fr": "Il faut que tu ___ patient.",
                "a": [
                  "sois"
                ],
                "hint": "être",
                "en": "You have to be patient."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Aller, faire, pouvoir, savoir, vouloir",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Aller* and *vouloir* go back to the regular stem for *nous, vous*: *que nous allions, que vous vouliez*. *Faire, pouvoir, savoir* keep the irregular stem everywhere: *que nous fassions, puissions, sachions*."
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "form",
                "verb": "faire",
                "tense": "subjonctif-present",
                "person": 0
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Il faut que tu sois à l'heure.",
                  "en": "You have to be on time."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Je ne crois pas qu'il ait raison.",
                  "en": "I don't think he's right."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il faut qu'on aille à la gare.",
                  "en": "We have to go to the station."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Je veux que vous fassiez attention.",
                  "en": "I want you to be careful."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
