    {
      "id": "sj-03-il-faut-que",
      "title": "Step 3: Il faut que: necessity",
      "fr": "il faut que + subjonctif",
      "level": "B1",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "subjunctive",
        "il faut que",
        "il est important que",
        "il vaut mieux que",
        "must",
        "have to"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "subjonctif-uses"
      ],
      "tense": "subjonctif-present",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Il faut que* + subjunctive = **someone** has to do something: *Il faut que je parte.* (I have to leave.) The same goes for *il est important que, il est nécessaire que, il vaut mieux que* (it's better that)."
            },
            {
              "type": "pattern",
              "rows": [
                {
                  "parts": [
                    [
                      "S",
                      "Il"
                    ],
                    [
                      "V",
                      "faut"
                    ],
                    [
                      "conj",
                      "que"
                    ],
                    [
                      "S",
                      "tu"
                    ],
                    [
                      "V",
                      "viennes."
                    ]
                  ],
                  "en": "You have to come."
                }
              ],
              "formula": [
                [
                  "S",
                  "il"
                ],
                [
                  "V",
                  "faut"
                ],
                [
                  "conj",
                  "que"
                ],
                "S",
                [
                  "V",
                  "subjonctif"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "With a person or in general",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "For a general rule, use the infinitive: *Il faut travailler.* (One has to work.) For a specific person, use *que* + subjunctive: *Il faut que tu travailles.* *Devoir* means the same: *Tu dois travailler.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "compare",
              "items": [
                {
                  "en": "One has to sleep.",
                  "fr": "Il faut [[dormir]]."
                },
                {
                  "en": "You have to sleep.",
                  "fr": "Il faut que tu [[dormes]]."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "cloze",
                "fr": "Il faut que je ___ mes devoirs.",
                "a": [
                  "fasse"
                ],
                "hint": "faire",
                "en": "I have to do my homework."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Il faut que nous partions à huit heures.",
                  "en": "We have to leave at eight."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il est important que vous soyez à l'heure.",
                  "en": "It's important that you're on time."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il vaut mieux que tu prennes un parapluie.",
                  "en": "You'd better take an umbrella."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il faut qu'on aille au supermarché.",
                  "en": "We have to go to the supermarket."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
