    {
      "id": "sj-04-wishes-feelings",
      "title": "Step 4: Wishes and feelings: je veux que, je suis content que",
      "fr": "le subjonctif après la volonté et les sentiments",
      "level": "B1",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "subjunctive",
        "je veux que",
        "vouloir que",
        "content que",
        "avoir peur que",
        "regretter que"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "subjonctif-uses"
      ],
      "tense": "subjonctif-present",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "After verbs of **wanting** (*vouloir que, aimer que, préférer que, souhaiter que*) and **feelings** (*être content que, être triste que, avoir peur que, regretter que, c'est dommage que*) the second verb is in the subjunctive, **when the two subjects are different**."
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "Whenever you mean *I want someone to...*, French needs *que* + subjunctive: *Je veux que tu viennes* (I want you to come).",
              "title": "A clue"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Same subject: infinitive",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "If both verbs have the same subject, there is no *que*, just the infinitive."
            },
            {
              "type": "compare",
              "items": [
                {
                  "en": "I want you to come.",
                  "wrong": "Je veux toi venir.",
                  "fr": "Je veux que tu [[viennes]]."
                },
                {
                  "en": "I want to come.",
                  "wrong": "Je veux que je vienne.",
                  "fr": "Je veux [[venir]]."
                },
                {
                  "en": "I'm happy that you're here.",
                  "fr": "Je suis content que tu [[sois]] là."
                },
                {
                  "en": "I'm happy to be here.",
                  "fr": "Je suis content [[d'être]] là."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "cloze",
                "fr": "Je veux que tu ___ avec moi.",
                "a": [
                  "viennes"
                ],
                "hint": "venir",
                "en": "I want you to come with me."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Mes parents veulent que je fasse mes devoirs.",
                  "en": "My parents want me to do my homework."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Je suis content que tu sois là.",
                  "en": "I'm glad you're here."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Elle a peur que son chien soit malade.",
                  "en": "She's afraid her dog is ill."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "C'est dommage qu'il pleuve.",
                  "en": "It's a pity it's raining."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Je préfère que vous veniez demain.",
                  "en": "I'd rather you came tomorrow."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
