    {
      "id": "sj-06-mix",
      "title": "Step 6: Subjunctive or indicative? Mixed practice",
      "fr": "subjonctif ou indicatif ?",
      "level": "B1",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "subjunctive",
        "indicative",
        "je pense que",
        "je ne pense pas que",
        "espérer que",
        "doute",
        "mix"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "subjonctif-uses",
        "subjonctif-conjunctions"
      ],
      "tense": "subjonctif-present",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Ask: is the second part a **fact**, or something you are **sure** of? Indicative. Is it **wanted, needed, felt, doubted or only possible**? Subjunctive. *Je pense qu'il vient* (I think so: indicative) but *Je ne pense pas qu'il vienne* (doubt: subjunctive)."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "indicative",
                "subjunctive"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "je pense que",
                  "je ne pense pas que"
                ],
                [
                  "je crois que",
                  "je doute que"
                ],
                [
                  "il est sûr que",
                  "il est possible que"
                ],
                [
                  "j'espère que",
                  "je souhaite que"
                ],
                [
                  "je sais que",
                  "je veux que"
                ],
                [
                  "parce que, quand, après que",
                  "pour que, avant que, bien que"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Watch out",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "*Espérer que* takes the **indicative**: *J'espère que tu vas bien.* It feels like a wish, but French treats it as an expectation."
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "*Penser* and *croire* take the indicative when you say yes (*Je crois qu'il est là*) and the subjunctive in the negative (*Je ne crois pas qu'il soit là*)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Je pense qu'elle a raison.",
                  "en": "I think she's right."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Je ne pense pas qu'elle ait raison.",
                  "en": "I don't think she's right."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "J'espère que tu viendras.",
                  "en": "I hope you'll come."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il est possible qu'il neige demain.",
                  "en": "It may snow tomorrow."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
